{"id":"bilhah","name":"Bilhah","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:bilhah"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Bilhah","text":"Faltering; bashful, Rachel’s handmaid, whom she gave to Jacob (Gen. 29:29). She was the mother of Dan and Naphtali (Gen. 30:3-8). Reuben was cursed by his father for committing adultry with her (35:22; 49:4). He was deprived of the birth-right, which was given to the sons of Joseph."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1090","lemma":"בִּלְהָה","xlit":"Bilhâh","gloss":"Bilhah, the name of one of Jacob's concubines","kjv":"Bilhah","count":10,"share":0.53},{"strong":"H7354","lemma":"רָחֵל","xlit":"Râchêl","gloss":"Rachel, a wife of Jacob","kjv":"Rachel","count":8,"share":0.42},{"strong":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","xlit":"Yaʻăqôb","gloss":"Jaakob, the Israelitish patriarch","kjv":"Jacob","count":8,"share":0.42},{"strong":"H6107","lemma":"עֶצֶם","xlit":"ʻEtsem","gloss":"Etsem, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Azem, Ezem","count":3,"share":0.16},{"strong":"H8198","lemma":"שִׁפְחָה","xlit":"shiphchâh","gloss":"a female slave","kjv":"maid, wench, bondwoman, womanservant","count":4,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","xlit":"yâlad","gloss":"to bear young","kjv":"bear, beget, birth, born","count":5,"share":0.26}],"verses":["Gen.29.29","Gen.30.3","Gen.30.4","Gen.30.5","Gen.30.7","Gen.35.22","Gen.35.25","Gen.37.2","Gen.46.25","1Chr.4.29","Gen.30.1","Gen.30.2","Gen.30.6","Gen.30.8","Gen.46.23","Gen.46.24","Gen.49.4","Josh.15.29","Josh.19.3"],"related":[{"id":"azem","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.158,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ezem","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.158,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"emulation","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.145,"why":"8 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"baalah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.143,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"rachel","type":"cooccur","shared":9,"jaccard":0.127,"why":"9 verses are i